  "body": "During testing my synapse installation I also wanted to add my email address to my account. I have a fully working Postfix environment and I gave it a try. Here are my current smtp settings:\r\n\r\n```\r\nemail:\r\n  smtp_host: \"my SMTP hostname\"\r\n  smpt_port: 578\r\n  smtp_user: \"my useraccount which works\"\r\n  smtp_pass: \"correct password\"\r\n  require_transport_security: true\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere is what Postfix thinks about it:\r\n```\r\n\r\nJun 30 13:28:04 ... postfix/smtpd[125295]: Anonymous TLS connection established from ...: TLSv1.3 with cipher TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 (256/256 bits) key-exchange X25519 server-signature RSA-PSS (4096 bits) server-digest SHA256\r\nJun 30 13:28:06 ... postfix/smtpd[125295]: warning: ...: SASL CRAM-MD5 authentication failed: \"some random noise here\"\r\nJun 30 13:28:06 ... postfix/smtpd[125295]: disconnect from ... ehlo=2 starttls=1 auth=0/1 quit=1 commands=4/5\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhy is Synapse trying to use CRAM-MD5? Its not enabled on my system and I am not going to enable it. We have LOGIN, PLAIN and TLS 1.3\r\n\r\nMy Synapse installation is up-to-date; installed via PIP and virtualenv, Python 3.9.5, Archlinux",
